Z||000000||1FST2M6||08-31-2001||08:47 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/turboDyno2.jpg">  <BR>178hp 217lbft<P>Fellow Fiero nut Predator (Donald) dove in head first with his PRESTINE 85 GT with only 24k miles. and got a Design one stage 2 turbo kit. well after the turbo flaked and a head did he was back on the road but with fuel delivery issues. Kevin at design one  gave him the run around for a while then ponied up a new and improved chip. well it's better but still starving a bit... with a rising rate fuel pressure riser being installed on the 7th-ish the shops Dyno tuner is confident Predator will see 200RWHP! <P>SWEET ride man! <BR>pics can be seen here... the Georgia Fieros Club page.<BR> <A HREF="http://fiero.freeyellow.com/DonaldHendrix.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero.freeyellow.com/DonaldHendrix.htm</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstmeatsig.jpg">            <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||08-31-2001||10:28 AM||||Those are my plans!  I want to do a turbo setup on my car either this or next winter.  I was going to put some stronger internals in, along with a cam, valves, springs, lifters and such.   I was lookin at lowering compression a little so I could get about 15lbs of boost.  It should be fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
